WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:04.067
Last clip you proved the mirror was
complete. Now open any account in it.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:07.067
Most C R Ms show you a value
and ask you to trust it.

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:10.700
Here you see what you know, why
you know it, and what happens next.

00:00:10.733 --> 00:00:13.567
In this clip you'll save a view
and read a company's timeline.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:17.200
You'll also trace a value to its source
and check the consent on a person.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.767
Sophia opens an account
before a renewal call,

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:21.467
and the employee count looks wrong.

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:25.367
In most tools she can't tell if it
came from a form, an import or a guess.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:26.433
Orbit can't either.

00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:29.700
So she checks by hand, and
she stops trusting the screen.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.233
Every value here can tell
you where it came from.

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:33.333
First, the lists.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:37.300
In the console: CRM, then Companies,
Contacts, Deals and Tasks.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:42.000
Companies and Contacts are tables
you can search, sort and filter.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.033
Deals are a pipeline board
and a table, by stage.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:48.833
Marking a deal lost asks for a loss
reason. It's never missing later.

00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:51.900
Tasks shows what is due, overdue and done.

00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:54.433
A saved view remembers a
list's filter and sort,

00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:56.900
so your team opens the
same slice the same way.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:00.367
Build one from any list, say every
tier A company with no owner.

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:04.267
If an agent changes a saved view,
the change goes through approval.

00:01:04.333 --> 00:01:05.500
Or ask your agent:

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:09.233
"Create a task for Mia to call the
champion at Northwind by Friday".

00:01:09.233 --> 00:01:12.833
It exists at once, because it only
touches your own organization.

00:01:12.833 --> 00:01:16.167
Then ask: "Save a view of every
tier A company with no owner".

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:19.600
That comes back as a proposal,
and a teammate approves it.

00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:24.000
Second, the company page, where
the story lives. Open any company.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.633
The overview comes first, then
tabs for contacts, deals, tasks,

00:01:27.633 --> 00:01:30.500
the Activity timeline,
Actions, Research and Evidence.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:34.667
The timeline puts every email, call,
meeting, signal and change in order,

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:36.867
so you read the account's
story from top to bottom.

00:01:36.867 --> 00:01:39.733
Page and agent read the same operations,

00:01:39.733 --> 00:01:43.800
so the console and the agent
can't disagree about an account.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.167
A relationship line says whether
your team already knows them.

00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:50.567
The Actions tab shows what the engines
drafted or did on this account:

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:54.100
the draft, the gate it passed,
who approved it, the outcome,

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:57.000
and an Undo where one exists.
Research holds sourced briefs.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Evidence collects each fact
with where it came from.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.233
A note or a call you log from
the page joins the timeline.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:05.367
Third, the part that sets this apart.

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:07.833
Next to any field, open Why this value.

00:02:07.833 --> 00:02:09.733
It shows which source wrote the value,

00:02:09.733 --> 00:02:12.767
which rule chose it when
sources disagreed, and when.

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.700
A lineage trace goes down
to the contributing records.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.300
A value a person set is marked as theirs,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.933
and it beats every automatic source.

00:02:19.933 --> 00:02:22.833
Power habit: open Why this
value before you edit.

00:02:22.833 --> 00:02:27.467
If a source got it wrong, fix the
source. If you set it by hand, it stays.

00:02:27.533 --> 00:02:31.600
Fourth, records beyond the big
three. In the console: CRM, Records.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:32.433
Browse every object type,

00:02:32.433 --> 00:02:36.633
including custom ones like a
Partner you defined in Model.

00:02:36.633 --> 00:02:39.767
Open a record to see its fields,
its provenance and its links.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:42.100
Contacts link to companies
through employment,

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.800
and deals link to contacts
with a buying role.

00:02:44.833 --> 00:02:48.567
On a contact, the Consent
tab lists email, phone, SMS,

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:52.233
WhatsApp and LinkedIn. Each shows
status, legal basis, source and expiry,

00:02:52.233 --> 00:02:54.333
with the history of every change.

00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:58.133
It's the record you'd hand over
in a data protection request.

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:01.000
The rules behind it come
in the clip called Consent,

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.700
suppression and privacy.

00:03:02.733 --> 00:03:04.300
Last, deals in your words.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:08.033
In the console: Settings,
Money, Your words for deals.

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:08.867
Types like new business,

00:03:08.867 --> 00:03:12.867
expansion or renewal use your
labels in every filter and grouping,

00:03:12.867 --> 00:03:13.733
never ours.

00:03:13.733 --> 00:03:17.433
A deal's page also shows its buying
committee: who plays which role,

00:03:17.433 --> 00:03:18.900
and whose is still missing.

00:03:18.967 --> 00:03:20.167
Or ask your agent:

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:23.733
"Show the Northwind company page and
explain why it is on the hot list".

00:03:23.733 --> 00:03:26.767
It answers from the same
records, with your permissions.

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:28.367
Each reason points at its evidence.

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:30.833
Open the company and
check the claim yourself.

00:03:30.867 --> 00:03:34.400
One more entry in the same rail:
AI chat. Ask about a record,

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.200
and anything it proposes to change
waits for a teammate's approval.

00:03:38.233 --> 00:03:42.233
Say it out loud: a tidy record page
is not the same as trust. Fair.

00:03:42.233 --> 00:03:43.367
So here's what backs it.

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:46.767
The agent reads with your permissions,
and can't see what you can't.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.933
Every reason points at
evidence you can open.

00:03:48.933 --> 00:03:51.767
A saved view change is
a proposal, not an edit.

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:54.733
And a sync can't overwrite
a value a person set.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.433
Boiled down: Work from
lists and saved views.

00:03:57.433 --> 00:04:00.933
Read the company page top to
bottom. Ask why for any value.

00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:03.233
Every value can tell
you where it came from.

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:05.500
You can open any account
and trust what you read,

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.000
because it shows its sources.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.400
Pick one company and open Why
this value on three fields.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:14.633
Next is identity and data quality,
where one customer becomes one record.
